City Engineer
 Description
Project would install an additional 60" or 72" diameter culvert under the Union Pacific Railroad at Dry Creek.
Project #
EN-14-012
 Justification
The existing culvert under the Union Pacific Railroad for Dry Creek is undersized, which results in water backing up behind the railroad
embankment.  To preclude the impacted area from getting any larger, the City Engineer's Office has imposed special (more restrictive) detention
requirements on the Dry Creek basin, which effectively reduces the amount of developable land.  Construction of this project would allow the
special detention requirements to be lifted.
